<task id="task-3607" class="- topic/topic task/task "><title class="- topic/title ">Removing assets from groups</title><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">Learn how to remove assets from groups.</shortdesc><prolog class="- topic/prolog "><author translate="no" type="creator" class="- topic/author ">Example Author &lt;author@example.com&gt;</author><metadata class="- topic/metadata "><prodinfo class="- topic/prodinfo "><prodname class="- topic/prodname "/><vrmlist class="- topic/vrmlist "><vrm modification="" release="" version="" class="- topic/vrm "/></vrmlist></prodinfo></metadata></prolog><taskbody class="- topic/body task/taskbody "><context class="- topic/section task/context "><p class="- topic/p ">Assets must be removed from groups on an individual basis. You cannot remove multiple assets from a group at the same time.</p></context><steps class="- topic/ol task/steps "><step product="classic-MyG" class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Navigate to the <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Assets</uicontrol> page in the main menu.</cmd></step><step conref="../../../Content_Warehouses/MyGeotab/Next-Gen_MyGeotab/Next-Gen_MyGeotab_Navigation_steps.dita#task-8836/step-3315" product="next-gen-MyG" class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd "/></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Select the asset you want to remove from a group to open the <ph conkeyref="varsMyGUI/AssetEditpage" class="- topic/ph "/> page.</cmd></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Under the <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Groups</uicontrol> dropdown list, click the <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">X</uicontrol> beside the group name to remove your asset from it. </cmd><info class="- topic/itemgroup task/info "><image href="../../Images/Groups_and_Rules/Adding_groups_to_an_asset.png" class="- topic/image "><alt class="- topic/alt ">The Asset Edit page showing the groups that are available to remove from an asset.</alt></image></info></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Save changes</uicontrol>.</cmd></step></steps><result class="- topic/section task/result ">Removing an asset from a group takes effect immediately.</result></taskbody></task>